---
source: src/cli/mod.rs, src/serve.rs, Cargo.toml
assertion: serve localhost foreground mode is a real one-shot adapter
schema:
  command: ee serve --foreground --json
  envelope: ee.response.v2
  payload: ee.serve.startup.v1
  status: foreground_one_shot
contracts:
  - ee serve --help is visible in default builds
  - ee serve --foreground --json binds a loopback listener when EE_SERVE_TOKEN is configured
  - startup output uses ee.response.v2 with data.schema ee.serve.startup.v1
  - one real TcpStream request is accepted and answered before foreground mode exits
  - ee serve without --foreground returns a usage error instead of implying background mode exists
  - no forbidden HTTP stack is introduced
  - serve adapter remains a wrapper boundary and must not add business logic
feature_requirements:
  - serve = [] feature flag in Cargo.toml
  - BuildFeature::new("serve", cfg!(feature = "serve")) in capabilities
  - FeatureEntry::new("serve", cfg!(feature = "serve"), "HTTP serve adapter")
  - forbidden dependencies not pulled: tokio, hyper, axum, tower, reqwest
  - top-level CLI command exists as an explicit foreground one-shot surface
evidence:
  - Cargo.toml: serve = []
  - src/cli/mod.rs: Command::Serve and handle_serve
  - src/serve.rs: serve_foreground_once, bind_serve_listener, render_serve_transport_exchange
  - tests/e2e_serve_localhost.rs: serve_foreground_cli_accepts_one_real_status_request
  - tests/fixtures/failure_modes/serve_unavailable_v1.json is retired
degraded_contract:
  - missing or weak EE_SERVE_TOKEN returns policy errors before binding
  - capabilities.features may still report the optional serve feature disabled
  - background serve mode is not claimed by the foreground one-shot adapter
